factrail is a clean Rust re-implementation of designs and rules first published,
under the MIT licence, in:

  * tamaratran/fast-jev-compaction — the Jev compaction method: two noul questions
    per tool call, the fitted history state, batching and decision thresholds.
    LICENSES/MIT-fast-jev-compaction.txt
  * deadczarvc-labs/jev-factkeep-compaction — fact rails: reproducible-read notes,
    fact stubs, rail tiers, the greedy per-result escalation, last-resort eviction,
    window pressure, saved full outputs and the secret families masked before saving.
    LICENSES/MIT-jev-factkeep-compaction.txt
  * deadczarvc/hermes-jev-compaction — the learned token-value model and its
    coefficients, the pooled fact budget with contained-token coverage, metadata
    egress, the deterministic no-model fallback and the hard eviction line.
    LICENSES/MIT-hermes-jev-compaction.txt

The agentbox estate policy (taint fence, switch, token trigger with hysteresis,
cache-warm compaction, scope, deadline, request redaction) comes from the
agentbox jev-compaction plugin (ADR-2093), by the same authors as this crate.

The Tev1 record format followed by the dataset export is documented in
togethercomputer/tev1 (MIT). No Tev1 code or data is included.
